## Store 6 (Stephenville) — adversarial map audit

### Pass 1 — Mechanical (rerun, not trusted from disk)
`./rebuild.sh 6` → exit 0. `report.json`: `verify: []`, `coverage: {sealed_floor_patches: [], unreachable_shelf_labels: []}`, `components: {n: 1, sizes: [52977]}`, 761 → 764 tests pass.

`walkable_pct` 20.1 is the fleet's lowest (peers 24.2–40.0), so I checked it rather than accepting it: the sales-floor boundary is 374–1111 × 60–715 pt = 45.7 % of the page (the left third of the page is the Curbside Parking drawing). Free floor is **43.9 % of the store footprint**, with 13.6 % sealed as BOH/service. Normal.

### Pass 2 — Systematic visual sweep
3×3 crops of `walkable_overlay.png` against a 2 px/pt render of PDF p.2, plus targeted zooms. All 7 printed pockets classified, **plus** the 4 sub-60-cell ones the stats do not print:

