Corridor continuity checked numerically, not just by eye: every aisle column runs 30.6–45.4 m unbroken; row scans at y=300/400/500 return **15 corridor runs from x 394 to 966** (one per badge); y=568 and y=660 are unbroken 436→1090; the east perimeter lane is unbroken y 182→478 through the Tortilleria mouth. Worst geodesic/euclidean detour on the whole floor is 1.41 — no swallowed corridor.

Unanchored departments inspected explicitly against `geometry.json`: **Market** (no anchor), **Tortilleria** (no anchor), Beer & Wine, Ice/Tobacco, Carts. `MEAT` and `KITCHEN` are false-positive anchors from the words "Canned Meat"/"Kitchen Gadgets"; `MEAT` is not in `SERVICE_DEPTS` so it spawns nothing, and `KITCHEN` is handled by `inclusions[0]`.

### Pass 3 — Label probes
Rotated text made per-span probing useless, so I probed per **word** bbox: **261 of 262** printed labels have reachable floor at 0.00 m. The single miss is `Pharmacy` (404,602) — the sealed dispensing room, correct.

### Passes 4–5
All 22 original `walk_truth` points pass and each lies inside the feature it names. Every config entry was ablation-tested and is load-bearing with an accurate WHY — including `exclusions[0]`, whose "2 pt / 0.18 m" claim I confirmed exactly against the raw grid (a one-cell-wide column at x=376, y 130–198), and which is what moves the RESTROOMS snap off y=160 onto the real door corridor at y=200.

