## Findings (all fixed)

**1 — Market department frontage had no `walk_truth` coverage.** (600, 205)
The band y 192–218 along the sawtooth south face of the two Market cases is the department's shopping side. Evidence: row scan y=190 → `(394,438) (490,528) (672,966)`, col x=610 → free `(192,218)`. This is the **only** department on the map with zero printed product labels, so neither the shelf-label net nor any existing point stands over it — precisely the store-24 shape. Fix: `walk_truth` must point.

**2 — The health-and-beauty short-aisle block had no `walk_truth` coverage.** (525, 620)
Five corridors at y 594–646, x 488–630, open at both ends. They sit **inside** the derived `auto:CHECKSTANDS` rect `[525.4, 586.6, 959.8, 723.5]` with `bridge: 20` — wide enough to bridge these ~19 pt corridors shut. Nothing in `walk_truth` was below y=580 in that block. Fix: `walk_truth` must point at the Vitamins label.

**3 — The north-wall back-of-house room had no `must_not`.** (500, 90)
The room at x 405–667, y 62–118 (staff double door at x≈567, swing door at x≈480) is blocked only because `extract.py` traced its rectangle as a fixture. `must_not (900,90)` covers the purple band east of it, not the room. Fix: `walk_truth` must_not point.

All three fixes are `walk_truth` points only — no `exclusions`/`inclusions`/`seal_zones` change was warranted, and no code, goldens, tests or other stores were touched. `./rebuild.sh 6` rerun after the edit: exit 0, `verify: []`, coverage empty, single component, 764 passed (+3, one per new point).

`AUDIT CLEAN — store 6 (3 findings fixed)`
